3Dos is a program that simulates a Dos command
line interface for the Psion Series 3 Computer. It will 
not run Dos programs, but all filing system commands
that are availible work. (See list of commands).

Shareware - This program is shareware. If you like it and want
to use it send $10 dollars to:
                        Mark Esposito
                        P.O. Box 741072
                        Houston Tx 77274-1072

New in Version 2.1
-------------------------------
	Better wildcard handling
        Additional command: [Move] will move a file
	to another location a delete the original.
        [Boot] will boot the 3link from the command line.
        [Link] will show the status of the 3link.
        Enhanced commands: (Mem, Dir, Del)
        New Online help
	Pc link - networks to Pc drives via Mclink
	Added application as an Opa
        File sizes will show up when you type in dir or dir/p, and
        Modification date will show up also. (looks more like Dos)
        Pop up calculator - 0 key or type in Calc
        Pic viewer lets you view images from the command line

In regards to this new Pc Link feature, Psion is to be 
commended in that this feature was added using only Opl/w.


Files included
----------------------
1. Dos.opa
2. 3Dos.doc
3. s3file.opo

Installation
-------------------
	Start out by creating a directory on your Series 3 
and call it Dos. It should be only 1 directory deep in the 
heirarchy. (like m:\Dos or A:\Dos or B:\Dos)
Copy the S3file.opo into the new \Dos directory or the 
\Oplhelp directory if you already have the Oplhelp application.
        Copy the Dos.opa file into any \app directory on the
Series 3.
        Next use Psion<I> to install application. Locate the
Dos.opa file and press enter.

Features:
----------

                -  Filing system Commands -

3Dos supports most Dos filing system commands. In this
version, it will also load Pc drives on to the Series 3 as 
networked drives. All file commands will work , so it is 
possible now to manipulate files on the Pc from the Series 3.

                - Mounting a Remote drive -

To mount a Pc drive use R plus the name of the drive. Like RC:
with a colon at the end. 3Dos supports drives A-Z, so if you have
a network loaded, they can be mounted also. You can also view the
Rom: drive built into the Series 3. (type in ROM: then dir)

** Note **

When copying files to a remote drive, you can't use
        Copy 3dos.doc RC:\
RC: is just a shortcut to mount the drive.
Use this instead:
        Copy 3dos.doc Rem::c:\

                - 3link auto booting -

The 3link comms link will automatically start up if plugged in
to the Series 3. To see the status type in Link from the command
line. If it says off, and you just plugged in the 3link cable,
type in "boot" and it will start up the link program.


                - Pop up Calculator -

A calculator is available by pressing 0 or typing in Calc. You can
use multiple operators.

                  - Move command -

Now you can move a file without having to delete the original. Just
type in "Move" from the command line, and 3dos will prompt you for the
file name. If the copy is successful it will delete the original.

                  - Online Help -

Online help is available. It is limited though. You need to know Dos
commands and how they work. The online help does however have a list
of commands that it supports.

                - Quiting 3dos -

To quit 3dos type in /X or /Exit or /bye.



Summary of Commands
----------------------------------------
About	(displays Pelican Software info window)
Boot    Boots the 3link software
Calc or 0   Starts pop up calculator
Cd/ - Cd\ - Cd..        (Chande directory -use either slash)
Chkdsk	(displays disk info about the current disk )
Cls	(Clear the screen)
Copy file1$ file2$ (no comma between filenames, like Dos)
Copy	(alone will bring up a Series 3 copy dialog)
Copy *.* drive:\  (copy all files in a directory to another drive)
** Note ** this copy command with wildcards doesn't want to work with
Remote drives - I'm still working on fixing this.
Date    (displays the date from the system clock)
Dir - Dir/w - Dir/p - Dir *.* - Dir .
Del  (alone will open a Series 3 delete dialog)
Del. or Del *.* (will delete all files in the current directory)
Del filename$
Del *.zip
/E  or 3 key  (Repeat last command - like F3 in Dos)
Format	(Formats a disk on the Series 3 - formatting
		must be turned on from the menu)
Free or Free drive$ (displays free space on requested drive)
Help or press Help key (displays help screen)
Md or Mkdir	(Creates a new directory)
Mem	(displays memory availible on all Series 3 devices)
Media	(displays the media type of current device)
Menu	or * (brings up the Series 3 pull down options window)
Off	(Turns Series 3 off)
Print or Pd	(prints current directory to a printer)
Rd or Rmdir	(Removes a directory - must be empty)
Ren	(used alone only - brings up a Series 3 dialog )
Time	(displays the time from the system clock)
Type	(types a file to the screen, even reads off the Pc)
Ver	(displays the 3Dos version)
View    (displays a pic file)
Vol     (displays volume name of current device)
/X /Exit /Bye - any of these will exit 3dos

CHANGING DRIVES:
-----------------------------------
Type in drive name to change drives.
        M: A: B: RA:-RZ:  Rom: (will show you the Rom drive)
Use RC: for the C:\ drive on the Pc if your are connected
to a remote Ibm compatible computer. RC: is short for 
REM::C:: which is how the Series 3 see's a remote 
Use R plus drive letter of drive you wish to mount on the 
Pc plus a colon.
If the drive doesn't exist or the Remote link is not connected 
or turned on, it will generate an error.

NOTES
-----------------

3Dos has some protection built in for data security.
	You cannot delete the root directory on the Pc.
	You cannot delete command.com on the Pc.
        You can turn on "query" to delete from the menu.
        Formatting capability is set off unless you turn it on.

Remember that these commands all work. You can 
delete files on the Pc from the Series 3.

***	Important	***

 if the Mclink program hangs up for any reason this
can cause the Series 3 to appear to be hung, or 
crashed. But chances are it's not. When it can't 
communicate it may wait for a while before it times
out. If this happens, which it should not, press the 
system button, press Psion<L> to turn off the remote
link, and the Series 3 should time out.


Setup:
        Press the menu key on the Psion and you can go to
        setup and set deleting and formatting options.


